  data: {
    LLM: '1. Players must match the pips of an open end of the linear layout.\n2. **Drawing**: If you cannot play, you MUST draw tiles from the boneyard one by one until you get a playable tile or the boneyard is empty.\n3. **Stock Limit**: In some traditional Hungarian rules, you cannot draw the very last tile of the boneyard.\n4. **End Game**: Once the boneyard is empty and a player cannot move, they must pass.',
    Player: '1. Players must match the pips of an open end of the linear layout.\n2. **Drawing**: If you cannot play, you MUST draw tiles from the boneyard one by one until you get a playable tile or the boneyard is empty.\n3. **Stock Limit**: In some traditional Hungarian rules, you cannot draw the very last tile of the boneyard.\n4. **End Game**: Once the boneyard is empty and a player cannot move, they must pass.',
    objective: 'Empty your hand of tiles or score lowest if the boneyard is empty and the game is blocked.',
    gameplay: '1. Players must match the pips of an open end of the linear layout.\n2. **Drawing**: If you cannot play, you MUST draw tiles from the boneyard one by one until you get a playable tile or the boneyard is empty.\n3. **Stock Limit**: In some traditional Hungarian rules, you cannot draw the very last tile of the boneyard.\n4. **End Game**: Once the boneyard is empty and a player cannot move, they must pass.',
    keyRules: [
      'Follow the legal action constraints defined for Hungarian DominÃ³ (Draw).',
      "Round outcome is resolved by the scoring method: The winner of the round scores the total pips from all opponents' hands.",
      'Winning condition: Empty your hand of tiles or score lowest if the boneyard is empty and the game is blocked.',
